---
title: 'Zoom Data Change Strategies'
description: 'Control how $framework chart zoom behaves when data is updated dynamically.'
enterprise: true
---

When chart data is updated dynamically, you may want to control how the zoom behaves. AG Charts provides several strategies to handle this through the `zoom.onDataChange` option.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Zoom Data Change Strategies" name="data-change-strategies" type="generated" /%}

Use the strategy selector and buttons to add data at the start, middle, or end of the dataset while zoomed in to observe how each strategy behaves differently.

## Strategies

The `zoom.onDataChange.strategy` option controls how the zoom adjusts when chart data changes:

```js format="snippet"
{
    zoom: {
        enabled: true,
        onDataChange: {
            strategy: 'preserveDomain',
        },
    },
    navigator: {
        enabled: true,
        miniChart: {
            enabled: true,
        },
    },
}
```

### Reset

When using `strategy: 'reset'`, the zoom is reset to show all data whenever the data changes.

**Use case:** Dashboards where users should always see the complete data range after updates.

### Preserve Ratios

When using `strategy: 'preserveRatios'`, the zoom ratios remain unchanged while the data is adjusted to fit within the current viewport.

**Use case:** When you want to maintain the same zoom percentage regardless of data changes.

### Preserve Domain

When using `strategy: 'preserveDomain'` (the default), the current axis domain (the actual values on the axis) is preserved when data changes.

**Use case:** Financial charts where users are analysing a specific time period and don't want their view disrupted by new data arriving.

## Comparing Strategies

The table below summarizes how each strategy behaves:

| Strategy         | Zoom Ratio     | Visible Domain   | Best For               |
| ---------------- | -------------- | ---------------- | ---------------------- |
| `reset`          | Resets to 100% | Shows all data   | Dashboards, overviews  |
| `preserveRatios` | Unchanged      | Shifts with data | Maintaining zoom level |
| `preserveDomain` | May change     | Unchanged        | Time-based analysis    |

## Live Streaming Data

For charts displaying live streaming data, you'll typically want to use `strategy: 'preserveRatios'` or `strategy: 'preserveDomain'` to prevent the view from jumping around as new data arrives.

{% chartExampleRunner title="Live Streaming" name="live-streaming" type="generated" /%}

In the example above:

-   New data points are added every second
-   The chart maintains the current view while new data streams in
-   Use the navigator's mini chart to see where you are in the full data range

## Stick to End

The `stickToEnd` option ensures that newly appended data stays visible when the user has panned to the very end of the data range. This is enabled by default (`true`).

{% chartExampleRunner title="Stick to End" name="stick-to-end" type="generated" /%}

```js format="snippet"
{
    zoom: {
        enabled: true,
        onDataChange: {
            strategy: 'preserveDomain',
            stickToEnd: true,
        },
    },
}
```

How it works:

1. When the chart is panned to the end of the data range and new data arrives, the view automatically scrolls to keep the new data visible
2. If the user has panned away from the end, the current `strategy` behaviour is used instead
3. Set `stickToEnd: false` to disable this behaviour and always use the strategy

**Use case:** Real-time monitoring dashboards where users want to follow the latest data as it arrives, but can also pan back to examine historical data without being interrupted.

